<title>GERMANY: Fazio declines comment on timing of EU meeting.</title>
<headline>Fazio declines comment on timing of EU meeting.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of Italy governor Antonio Fazio declined to comment on when Rome's request for the lira to re-enter Europe's Exchange Rate Mechanism (ERM) would be considered.</p>
<p>Asked whether Italy's application for re-entry meant that a meeting of the European monetary committee meeting would take place on Saturday, as sources had told Reuters, he said &quot;No comment. The minister (Italian Treasury minister Ciampi) can tell you about that.&quot;</p>
<p>When pressed further to comment on the possibility of the meeting, he added &quot;Just wait and see.&quot;</p>
<p>Fazio was in Frankfurt for the European Banking Congress.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
